    "teach_3": {
      "id": "teach_3",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Here is where cube identities shine brightest.\n\na^3 + b^3 = (a + b)(a^2 − ab + b^2)\n\nSo a fraction like:\n\n(25^3 + 15^3)/(25^2 − 25 × 15 + 15^2)\n\nhas the whole bottom hiding inside the top.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_3_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_3_step": {
      "id": "teach_3_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Cancel the common bracket:\n\n= (a + b)(a^2 − ab + b^2)/(a^2 − ab + b^2)\n= a + b\n= 25 + 15 = 40\n\nNever cube the numbers. Recognise the shape and cancel.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_3"
        }
      ]
    },
