    "teach_4": {
      "id": "teach_4",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "The minus version, straight from the book:\n\na^3 − b^3 = (a − b)(a^2 + ab + b^2)\n\nNotice the bottom changes: minus in the cube, PLUS ab in the bracket.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_4_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_4_step": {
      "id": "teach_4_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "So:\n\n(343^3 − 113^3)/(343^2 + 343 × 113 + 113^2)\n= a − b\n= 343 − 113\n= 230\n\nRead the denominator carefully: a^2 + ab + b^2 pairs with a^3 − b^3. The sign flip is the exam's favourite confusion.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_4"
        }
      ]
    },
